---
/**
 * VAT Calculator UK — 영국판 제도 도구(basis "law"). 한국어판 부가세(/vat/)와 세율·끝수 규칙이 달라 짝(hreflang)을 맺지 않는다
 * (조사표 영국 칸 '제도').
 * 계산은 lib/gb/vat.ts(정수 펜스), 화면은 lib/gb/vat-ui.ts, 숫자는 rates/gb/vat-2026.json
 * (GOV.UK VAT rates · HMRC VAT Notice 700 7.3.1·17.5·17.5.1·17.6, Last updated 25 June 2026 — 2026-10-21 확인).
 *
 * 소제목은 영국 구글 자동완성에서 왔다(keywords/gb-vat-2026-10-21.csv, hl en · gl gb):
 *   how to calculate vat uk · from net / remove vat from price·from gross·formula / reverse vat calculator·calculator backwards /
 *   vat 20 percent · vat 5 percent / add vat formula excel · remove vat excel formula / vat 2026 uk
 * 쓰지 않는 것(이번 회차 원문을 읽지 않음): 어느 품목이 몇 %인지 판정, 등록 기준액, reverse charge(construction·CIS),
 * 북아일랜드·스코틀랜드 별도 규칙 여부, 소매 scheme, 마일리지 VAT. 'reverse vat' 검색어는 '거꾸로 계산'으로만 다룬다.
 */
import BaseHead from "../../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import AdSlot from "../../../components/AdSlot.astro";
import ClarityHead from "../../../components/ClarityHead.astro";
import GtagHead from "../../../components/GtagHead.astro";
import TrackLinks from "../../../components/TrackLinks.astro";
import AdSenseHead from "../../../components/AdSenseHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { fromNet, fromGross, gbp, STANDARD, REDUCED } from "../../../lib/gb/vat";
import "../../../styles/global.css";

const title = "VAT Calculator UK — Add or Remove VAT at 20% or 5% (HMRC VAT Fraction)";
const description =
  "Add VAT to a net price or remove VAT from a gross price at the UK standard rate of 20% or reduced rate of 5%, using HMRC's VAT fraction (1/6, 1/21) and penny rounding.";

const net100 = fromNet(10000, STANDARD);
const net100r = fromNet(10000, REDUCED);
const notice = fromGross(240, STANDARD);
const gross120 = fromGross(12000, STANDARD);
const gross105 = fromGross(10500, REDUCED);
const ten = { nearest: fromGross(1000, STANDARD, "nearest"), down: fromGross(1000, STANDARD, "down") };
const odd = { nearest: fromNet(1099, STANDARD, "nearest"), down: fromNet(1099, STANDARD, "down") };
---

<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
    <ClarityHead />
    <GtagHead />
    <AdSenseHead />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-texture">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <h1>VAT Calculator UK</h1>
      <p>
        Type a price, choose whether it already includes VAT, and pick the rate. The calculator shows the price excluding VAT, the
        VAT itself and the price including VAT. The rates are the ones GOV.UK lists: the standard rate of {STANDARD}% and the reduced
        rate of {REDUCED}%.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="vt-mode">What do you want to do?</label>
          <select id="vt-mode" data-seg>
            <option value="add" selected>Add VAT</option>
            <option value="remove">Remove VAT</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="vt-rate">VAT rate</label>
          <select id="vt-rate" data-seg>
            <option value="20" selected>20% standard</option>
            <option value="5">5% reduced</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label id="vt-input-label" for="vt-amount">Price excluding VAT (£)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="decimal" id="vt-amount" value="100.00" autocomplete="off" data-ui="off" />
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="vt-round">Fractions of a penny</label>
          <select id="vt-round" data-seg>
            <option value="nearest" selected>Nearest penny</option>
            <option value="down">Round down</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="result-hero" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-dock="hero-value" data-bar="out-net,out-vat">
          <p class="label" id="hero-label">Price including VAT</p>
          <p class="big" id="hero-value">{gbp(net100.gross)}</p>
          <p class="hint" id="vt-formula">VAT = {gbp(10000)} × 20% (rounded to the nearest penny)</p>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-row" data-receipt>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Excluding VAT</span>
            <span class="value" id="out-net">{gbp(net100.net)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label" id="vat-label">VAT (20%)</span>
            <span class="value" id="out-vat">{gbp(net100.vat)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Including VAT</span>
            <span class="value" id="out-gross">{gbp(net100.gross)}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
          <button id="btn-download" type="button">Save as image</button>
          <button id="btn-share" type="button" class="secondary">Share</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How to calculate VAT in the UK</h2>
      <p>
        To add VAT to a net price, multiply the price by the rate and add the result: VAT = net price × 20%, gross price = net price
        + VAT. On {gbp(10000)}, VAT at 20% is {gbp(net100.vat)}, so the price including VAT is {gbp(net100.gross)}. At the 5% reduced
        rate it is {gbp(net100r.gross)}.
      </p>

      <h2>How to remove VAT from a price (working VAT out backwards)</h2>
      <p>
        When VAT is already in the price, taking 20% of the price gives the wrong answer. HMRC's VAT Notice 700 (paragraph 7.3.1)
        uses the <strong>VAT fraction</strong> instead: the rate divided by 100 plus the rate.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>20%</strong> — 20/120, which is one-sixth. VAT = gross price ÷ 6.</li>
        <li><strong>5%</strong> — 5/105, which is one twenty-first. VAT = gross price ÷ 21.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        HMRC's own example: something sold for {gbp(240)} at 20% contains {gbp(notice.vat)} of VAT — one-sixth of {gbp(240)}, not 20%
        of it — leaving {gbp(notice.net)} before VAT. In the same way {gbp(12000)} including VAT is {gbp(gross120.net)} plus
        {gbp(gross120.vat)} VAT, and {gbp(10500)} at 5% is {gbp(gross105.net)} plus {gbp(gross105.vat)} VAT. Dividing by 1.2 also gives
        the net price; this calculator works out the VAT first and takes it away from the price you typed, so the three figures always
        add up.
      </p>

      <h2>VAT at 20% and 5% — which rate?</h2>
      <p>
        GOV.UK describes the three rates like this: the standard rate of 20% for most goods and services, the reduced rate of 5% for
        some goods and services such as children's car seats and home energy, and the zero rate of 0% for zero-rated goods and services
        such as most food and children's clothes. At 0% there is no VAT to add or remove.
      </p>
      <p>
        This calculator does not decide which rate applies to a particular product or service. Check the GOV.UK rates page and HMRC's
        guidance for that.
      </p>

      <h2>Rounding: nearest penny or round down?</h2>
      <p>
        VAT often comes out with fractions of a penny. VAT Notice 700 says that on a VAT invoice you may round the total VAT down to a
        whole penny (paragraph 17.5), and that if you work out VAT line by line you can round to the nearest 1p or 0.5p, or down to the
        nearest 0.1p, as long as you are consistent (17.5.1). It also notes that the round-down concession is meant for invoice
        traders, and that retailers who work out VAT at line or invoice level must not round the VAT down (17.6).
      </p>
      <p>
        For example, VAT in {gbp(1000)} at 20% is 1,000p ÷ 6 = 166.66…p: {gbp(ten.nearest.vat)} to the nearest penny (net
        {gbp(ten.nearest.net)}), or {gbp(ten.down.vat)} rounded down (net {gbp(ten.down.net)}). Adding VAT to {gbp(1099)} gives
        219.8p: {gbp(odd.nearest.vat)} to the nearest penny, {gbp(odd.down.vat)} rounded down. The calculator starts on "Nearest penny"
        — that is just the page's default setting, not an HMRC rule.
      </p>

      <h2>VAT formulas for Excel or Google Sheets</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Add VAT at 20% (price in A1): <code>=A1+ROUND(A1*20%,2)</code></li>
        <li>VAT inside a gross price at 20%: <code>=ROUND(A1/6,2)</code>, and the net price <code>=A1-ROUND(A1/6,2)</code></li>
        <li>For 5%, use <code>A1*5%</code> and <code>A1/21</code>. Replace <code>ROUND</code> with <code>ROUNDDOWN</code> to round down.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        On a calculator: {gbp(10000)} <kbd>×</kbd> <kbd>1.2</kbd> adds 20% VAT, and {gbp(12000)} <kbd>÷</kbd> <kbd>6</kbd> gives the VAT
        inside a gross price.
      </p>

      <details>
        <summary>What is the VAT rate in the UK in 2026?</summary>
        <p>
          The standard rate is 20%, the reduced rate 5% and the zero rate 0%. GOV.UK notes that the standard rate went up to 20% on
          4 January 2011, from 17.5%. When we checked the GOV.UK rates page on 21 October 2026 it did not mention any planned change.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is "reverse VAT" the same as the reverse charge?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Here "reverse" just means working backwards from a price that includes VAT. The VAT reverse charge is a different
          subject, and this calculator does not deal with it — see HMRC's guidance on GOV.UK.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why isn't the VAT on a VAT-inclusive price 20% of it?</summary>
        <p>
          Because 20% was added to the net price, not to the gross one. {gbp(12000)} is {gbp(10000)} plus 20% of {gbp(10000)}, so the
          VAT is {gbp(2000)} — one-sixth of {gbp(12000)}, not 20% of it ({gbp(2400)}).
        </p>
      </details>

      <p>
        Related: <a href="/en-gb/tools/percent/">percentage calculator</a> for discounts and percentage increases.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/vat-rates" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GOV.UK — VAT rates</a> (checked 21 October 2026)</li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/vat-guide-notice-700" rel="noopener" target="_blank">HMRC — VAT guide (VAT Notice 700)</a>,
          paragraphs 7.3.1, 17.5, 17.5.1 and 17.6 (last updated 25 June 2026, checked 21 October 2026)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot label="vat-result-en-gb" />
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
    <script src="../../../lib/gb/vat-ui.ts"></script>
    <TrackLinks />
    <script src="../../../scripts/calc-ui.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
